# DevOpsAssignment_Group05
The daily DevOps Git workflow follows a linear sequence to move code from local development to production pipelines:

git clone: Creates a local copy of a remote repository. 
git add .: Stages all new and changed files for the next commit. 
git commit -m: Saves the staged changes with a descriptive message. 
git push -u origin: Uploads local commits to the remote repository and sets upstream tracking. 
git pull: Fetches and merges the latest changes from the remote repository into the local branch. 


Core CLI Commands

opencode [project]: Launches the interactive Text User Interface (TUI) in the specified directory. 
opencode run [message]: Executes a one-shot, non-interactive prompt and exits; supports flags like --continue or --session to resume previous contexts. 
opencode serve: Starts a headless HTTP API server for remote access. 
opencode web: Launches a headless server with a web-based UI. 
Management and Configuration

opencode auth: Manages provider credentials and login flows (e.g., opencode auth login --provider anthropic). 
opencode models [provider]: Lists available LLM models, optionally filtered by provider.
opencode mcp: Manages Model Context Protocol servers, including adding, listing, and authenticating connections. 
opencode session: Lists, deletes, or manages conversation history and IDs. 
opencode upgrade: Updates OpenCode via various package managers (npm, brew, curl, etc.). 
TUI Slash Commands
Inside the interactive interface, users can type / to access built-in shortcuts:

/init: Generates or updates AGENTS.md for project context. 
/help: Displays available commands and keybindings. 
/share: Generates a public URL for the current session. 
/undo / /redo: Reverts or re-applies the agent's last actions. 
/connect: Manages model provider connections. 
